  description = {Bandicota bengalensis (Gray \& Hardwicke).  Etymologically, ``brown as a Kokila''.  \cite[\#4324]{CDIAL} relates \emph{kokila}  to \emph{golaka} but it may more likely be a Dravidian loanword from \emph{koko, kogi, koki}, meaning ``small, little, young'' \cite[2030]{DED}.  This is possibly supported by Kannada \emph{kok} and Telugu \emph{golatta, koku} for the mole-rat, reported by \citet[205]{bia}},
