@Entry{haṃsa,
  citationkey = {haṃsa},
  description = {Cygnus olor, Gmelin, \cite[ch.\,84]{dave}. As Dave says, "a generic term for a large part of the Anatidae family" including Swans, Geese, Ducks and Teals.  The term needs to be translated variously according to the geographical context of  the usage.  In the Himalayan region, ``swan" is appropriate, but in more southerly peninsular India, ``goose'' is more likely.  The dogmatism of \cite{voge-1962} is based on mainly southern observations and temple carvings.  The discussion by \cite{dave} is nuanced and accurate},
